# http_test again, with the e2e tier on: BEADS_TEST_EMBEDDED_DOLT=1 starts the
# in-process server over embedded Dolt and BEADS_HTTP_TEST_REQUIRED=1 turns a
# skip of that tier into a failure. http_test alone skips the TestE2E_* cases
# in every lane, because no lane sets those variables for it. It repeats
# http_test's `env` (go_test_pinned_shard.sh, like go_test_variant.sh, does
# not inherit it).
#
# Shard count: the package's tests are serial. The 32 TestE2E_* cases
# measured at >= 3s are pinned (tools/bazel/go_test_pinned_shard.sh,
# served_pinned_shards.txt from tools/bazel/pin_shards.py --shards 10
# --min-seconds 3 --record-measured --tests-in backend/http) onto 10 shards,
# and the binary's round-robin deals every other test over the last 4: the
# 30 the manifest lists rr (about a second together) and any test added
# since. The
# durations are each test's maximum over 35 PR runs of the lane on
# 2026-10-23..24 (bazel.yml's bazel-embedded-served-testxml artifact, 29
# distinct executions of each shard): 18-174s a test. The slowest,
# TestE2E_BlockedFlagsOverHTTP (117s median), alone sets the longest shard;
# replayed over those runs the longest shard takes ~125s at the median run
# and ~143s at p90. The same test's time varies 2-4x between runs with the
# executors' load, so size the pins from sharded CI runs of the lane, never
# from a local one.
# With one round-robin shard (shard_count 7, pins of 2026-10-13) every test
# added later landed in it, and by 2026-10-23 it ran 314-633s, the lane's
# last action. scripts/pinned_shards_sources_test.go fails once more than 2
# tests per round-robin shard are listed neither pinned nor rr (added since
# the measurement), and prints the command that regenerates the manifest
# (needs gh and the network; --tests-in drops what the runs measured that
# this checkout does not define, renamed or other branches' tests):
#   python3 tools/bazel/pin_shards.py --shards 10 --min-seconds 3 \
#       --record-measured --tests-in backend/http \
#       --write backend/http/served_pinned_shards.txt \
#       $(tools/bazel/fetch_served_testxml.sh 30 "$(mktemp -d)")
#
# Tags:
#   embedded: the embedded-Dolt tier; excluded from --config=prcore/ci,
#     selected by --config=embedded.
sh_test(
    name = "http_served_test",
    size = "large",
    # -test.timeout=19m fires (with a goroutine dump) before Bazel's 1200s
    # action limit (eternal under --config=embedded).
    timeout = "eternal",
    srcs = ["//tools/bazel:go_test_pinned_shard.sh"],
    args = [
        "$(rootpath :served_pinned_shards.txt)",
        "$(rootpath :http_test)",
        "-test.v",
        "-test.count=1",
        "-test.timeout=19m",
    ],
    data = [
        "served_pinned_shards.txt",
        ":http_test",
        "//cmd/bd:bd_for_tests",
    ],
    env = {
        "BEADS_HTTP_TEST_REQUIRED": "1",
        "BEADS_TEST_BD_BINARY": "$(rlocationpath //cmd/bd:bd_for_tests)",
        "BEADS_TEST_EMBEDDED_DOLT": "1",
    },
    shard_count = 14,
    tags = ["embedded"],
)

